hash.c: the same entry slots under PoisonCap, under MRB_POISONCAP_HASH (4.0.0-rc2).

The second mechanism at the level patch 0010 sublets, so the two can be measured against
one defect set on one platform. Nothing changes without the define; the arm builds for
CheriBSD purecap with the PoisonCap SDK and is selected at run time by MRB_POISON_MODE.

WHAT IT MEASURES, AND WHY IT EXISTS

0010's header says the level exists because a slot is vacated by entry_delete() and
refilled by a later ea_set() with nothing released to the allocator in between, so
revocation keyed to free() has nothing to fire on. That was an argument. This patch makes
it a measurement, and the measurement corrected the argument:

  - On CheriBSD purecap at this pin, with libc revocation OFF and again ON
    (_RUNTIME_REVOCATION_ENABLE=1), all three reuse-not-free defects reproduce unchanged.
    Revocation at the malloc/free interface makes no difference to any of them, because
    no free() is ever called. That is the claim, now measured rather than asserted.
  - With the per-slot adapter below, PoisonCap catches three of them. So the mechanism is
    NOT blind to the class -- what it needs is hooks at the nested level, which is exactly
    what Sublet needs too. The level is the finding, not the primitive.

THE ARM, AND WHAT DIFFERS FROM 0010

The level, the event and the two invariants are 0010's. Only the taking-back differs:

    0010  sublet_take / sublet_give on a node split out of a linear region
    here  an exactly-bounded alias per slot, and at slot death cpoison over the slot's
          16-byte lines, one synchronous cheri_revoke sweep, cclearpoison, zero

MRB_POISON_MODE=0 publishes and never invalidates; =1 invalidates at slot death. Poison,
sweep and clear are separate calls so a drop of many slots pays ONE sweep, while
revocation is still complete before the caller returns.

Per-slot poison is sound where a whole-span poison would not be: a slot's alias is bounded
to its own sizeof(hash_entry) bytes, so poisoning slot i intersects slot i's alias and no
other. Surviving slots keep theirs, which is why nothing has to be re-published and the
hash never re-fetches its array pointer -- the difference from the APR node adapter
(ports/apr/pools/src/cheribsd/node-poison.c), which poisons a whole node and republishes it.

THE CONTROL HAD TO BE FIXED BEFORE IT MEASURED ANYTHING, TWICE

Both errors made mode 1 look better than it is, and both are why liveness lives in live[]
rather than in the alias slot:

 1. A vacated slot returned NULL from ea_get(), so a re-read faulted on the NULL rather
    than on anything revoked. Mode 0 then faulted on a54353ecf and on eb7693857's rehash-ht,
    which pristine purecap runs to completion -- an artifact of the sidecar counted as a catch.
 2. With NULL gone from mode 0 but kept in mode 1, a mode-1 fault still could not be
    attributed to revocation: a NULL dereference on purecap raises the same in-address-space
    security exception as a revoked capability, with the same message. So NEITHER mode stores
    NULL. Mode 0 hands back a valid alias for a vacated slot (upstream behaviour under
    per-slot bounds); mode 1 hands back the same alias after the sweep has revoked it. The
    pair then differs in one variable, the sweep, and nothing else.

MEASURED (CheriBSD purecap, pver-214a1a2d9, guest revocation default 0)

  instrument      hash-sanity -- births, deaths, compaction, AR->HT growth, dup, free --
                  PASSES in both modes, issued=released=917, sweeps 0 (m0) vs 278 (m1).
                  The mechanism fires and does not break the interpreter.
  caught          m0 completes, m1 faults: a54353ecf, 08a0432d1, and eb7693857's inspect,
                  rehash-ar and rehash-ht paths.
  already spatial CHERI bounds alone fault on 4663fef45's h[]/key?/[]= paths and on
                  eb7693857's __except path, on PRISTINE upstream -- no adapter involved.
                  These are out-of-bounds reads, so they are not this level's to claim.
  missed          4663fef45's indexed-shape path (m1 sweeps=23, still NO_RAISE), and
                  1c57532b2, which is the shared-string-buffer level and has no adapter
                  in either mechanism.

LIMITS, STATED

The sub-case split that separates "caught here" from "CHERI already had it" was run for
this arm. The Sublet arm's published tally is at WHOLE-CASE granularity, so the two are not
yet a like-for-like head-to-head; that re-measurement is open. entry_delete() keeps its
signature, so the slot is found by searching the live spans, as in 0010. XP_MAX spans and
XP_SLOTS slots bound what is covered; past either, ea_resize falls back to malloc and the
array is simply not covered rather than failing. Dropped spans keep their mapping and are
reused, which bounds the process at XP_MAX pages and is safe because a drop revokes every
slot in the span.

